{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-27781",
  "enisaUuid": "c49c8354-486e-3f40-a4e3-4dc50d20708b",
  "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: cpsw_new: Fix potential unregister of netdev that has not been registered yet\n\nIf an error occurs during register_netdev() for the first MAC in\ncpsw_register_ports(), even though cpsw->slaves[0].ndev is set to NULL,\ncpsw->slaves[1].ndev would remain unchanged. This could later cause\ncpsw_unregister_ports() to attempt unregistering the second MAC.\nTo address this, add a check for ndev->reg_state before calling\nunregister_netdev(). With this change, setting cpsw->slaves[i].ndev\nto NULL becomes unnecessary and can be removed accordingly.",
  "datePublished": "May 6, 2026, 11:28:20 AM",
  "dateUpdated": "Jul 4, 2026, 11:50:36 AM",
  "baseScore": 0.0,
  "references": "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/da8e1623a3028e1d8c75eec7898d94c6f17dce40\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d31a12cee10bbc12b4b523a4709fd1fdee8b7d0f\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23acc565186ee27e788408cbd81b92730b6aaa3a\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/67cca9df4d17f2c824655d31195b2e75334ae286\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14645799ad5253a028cf662e2f9cd18a68f74b31\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29739ec197ed66535bc0b86f14ab66c5f4512138\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/349c4cac6f54a81fc107589771f88136a2b20415\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d724b34fbe13b71865ad0906a4be97571f19cf5\n",
